# Routes vs feature views vs ui/ components

When adding or moving Svelte UI, follow this split. **If placement is unclear, use AskQuestion before creating files.**

## 1. Routes (`src/routes/`)

- **URL = folder path.** Use SvelteKit names: `+page.svelte`, `+layout.svelte`, `+server.ts`.
- **Keep `+page.svelte` thin** — import a view from `lib/`, do not build full screens inline.
- Do **not** suffix route files with `-page`; the folder already defines the page.

```svelte
<!-- src/routes/history/+page.svelte -->
<script lang="ts">
  import HistoryPage from '$lib/components/history/history-page.svelte';
</script>
<HistoryPage />
```

## 2. Feature / area views (`src/lib/components/<area>/`)

- One subdirectory per product area: `home/`, `history/`, `chat/`, `editor/`, `shell/`, …
- **Domain context lives here:** copy, example data, wiring to stores/API, page-specific layout.
- Name by **feature**, not route mechanics (`start-learning-session.svelte`, not `home-route.svelte`).
- Optional `-page` suffix on lib components only when it helps signal “single-route view” (e.g. `history-page.svelte`).

## 3. Generic UI (`src/lib/components/ui/`)

- **Domain-agnostic** building blocks aligned with **shadcn-svelte** (Button, Card, Dialog, …).
- Compose from existing shadcn primitives before raw `<button>` / custom markup; add new shadcn components via `pnpm dlx shadcn-svelte@latest add <name>` when needed.
- **Props in, events out** — no hardcoded product strings, example lists, or API calls.
- Parent/feature component supplies labels, items, and handlers.

```svelte
<!-- ✅ ui/chip/chip-grid.svelte — generic; parent supplies ChipItem { label, prompt } -->
<ChipGrid items={HOME_EXAMPLE_PROMPTS} onSelect={fillPrompt} />

<!-- ❌ ui/ — hardcoded example lists or product copy inside ChipGrid -->
```

## 4. Static assets (`src/lib/assets/`)

- Logos, icons, illustrations as `.svg` / images — import in feature views.
- No Svelte wrapper unless the asset needs dynamic props or theme binding via CSS variables.

## 5. Before creating a component — checklist

| Question | If yes → |
|----------|----------|
| Tied to one URL/screen and product copy? | `lib/components/<area>/` |
| Reusable on multiple screens, no domain text? | `lib/components/ui/` |
| Only maps a URL to a view? | `routes/.../+page.svelte` (thin) |
| Static image/logo? | `lib/assets/` |

**Unclear?** Ask the user (area name, ui vs feature, route) — do not guess and drop files in the wrong folder.

See **ADR-016** in `docs/decisions.md` for full context.
